  "id": "psychological-resilience",
  "term": "psychological resilience",
  "definition": "Psychological resilience is a person’s ability to stay relatively stable and adapt in constructive ways when facing adversity or stress. Higher resilience is associated with more balanced emotional responses under stress and may support positive development and prosocial behavior.",
